<title>UK: Major says expects low UK inflation.</title>
<headline>Major says expects low UK inflation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Prime Minister John Major said on Thursday he expects the country to continue to enjoy a period of low inflation.</p>
<p>He was speaking after offcial figures showed British core inflation in March stood at 2.7 percent.</p>
<p>He told a news conference that Britain was enjoying &quot;the longest period of low inflation for 50 years and I expect that to continue.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44 171 542 7947</p>
